0263-negroni-wlan-stages: Wi-Fi driver levels (boot-arg negroniwlan=N), step lines, DMA-path check.
Level 2 = steps 1-8 (BAR0, firmware, pool, DMA path, PBL, BHI SBL), 3 = steps 9-12 (MHI READY, MMIO,
M0, EE SBL), 4 = steps 13-15 (BHIe, EE AMSS, IPCR channels). "NEGRONI WLAN: step N NAME" before each
step, "... failed: REASON" on an error, badge WLAN N / OK / STOP, BHI heartbeat each second, MHI window
0..36-bit (cnss2 pci.c:5509), M1 -> device-wake toggle (pm.c:334-363), RDDM stop. Step 6 reports the GCC
NoC/TBU branches (CLK_OFF is not trusted: BRANCH_HALT_SKIP + hwcg) and stops only on a clear vote bit
(0x62000 bit 12/19); it reads the apps SMMU (stream 0x1c01) and skips the scan when EXIDS is set.
negroniwlan_smmu=1 default (stop on a sure fault), 0 report only, 2 writes a bypass SMR/S2CR (owner
approval needed). Review fixes 2026-10-26 applied. Panic fix 2026-10-26: every apps-SMMU access uses
negroni_mmio_rd32/wr32 (0255; the hypervisor injected an SEA on the post-index SMR scan load). Details:
patches/xnu/README-wifi.md "0263".

